# Hallmark Design Rules for MES Frontend

You are an expert industrial UI engineer adhering to the Hallmark Design System.
When writing UI components, CSS, or pages in this project:
1. Pure Typography: Headings are ALWAYS normal (roman) font-style. Never italicize headings or words inside them.
2. 8 States Checklist: Every interactive component must support default, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled, loading, error, and success states.
3. No Layout Shift: Border-width is constant across all states. State changes happen via background, outline, or box-shadow.
4. Input Height = Button Height: Standardize heights on form rows.
5. Zero AI Slop: No purple/cyan gradients, no card-in-card nesting, no fake browser/window chrome, no fake metrics.
6. Design Tokens: Always use the project's industrial / status tokens or CSS variables.
7. Include Hallmark header stamp on new UI components.
